WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.100
-I'm psyched about this.
I couldn't wait to read it.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.734
I couldn't wait to have you
on to talk about it.

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:07.701
"Waxing On." Congrats on this.
-Thank you, man.

00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:10.734
-What was it like
to write a full-on memoir?

00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:16.467
-Well, you know, I wanted to
dive into telling the story of

00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:18.801
walking in the shoes of
this Daniel LaRusso character

00:00:18.801 --> 00:00:21.267
and everything
I've gained from it.

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:23.934
And the -- It's equal parts

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:25.934
nostalgia and
contemporary relevance.

00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:30.400
It's very unique to have
something that I made in 1983

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.300
that is relevant today because
you folks won't let it go away,

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:33.467
and it's awesome.

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:36.634
-Yeah, exactly. It's fantastic.
-And so...

00:00:36.634 --> 00:00:37.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:41.100
Yeah, so, I wrote it
during season 4 and 5

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.334
of shooting "Cobra Kai."

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:44.801
We were --
It was during the pandemic,

00:00:44.801 --> 00:00:48.100
so I had my lockdown times,
ordering room service

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.000
and sort of going through
the emotional ups and downs

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.267
of the making of the film,

00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:54.267
the behind-the-scenes
untold stories,

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:57.033
the launch of the summer of '84,

00:00:57.033 --> 00:00:58.868
what that was like for me
and the afterlife.

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:02.934
And it's a celebration of
that movie

00:01:02.934 --> 00:01:04.534
and pop culture
and cinema and my life.

00:01:04.534 --> 00:01:07.367
-Also, I want to hear all
the great stories, too.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:10.400
I know in here, there's
the audition for "Karate Kid,"

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.100
which I love that you wore a
Tom Petty sweatshirt.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.434
-Yes, I did.

00:01:13.434 --> 00:01:15.634
Well, the thing with
the Tom Petty sweatshirt --

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:17.367
And a Members Only jacket.

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:20.767
So if I had a mullet, I would
have been the poster child --

00:01:20.767 --> 00:01:22.234
-For the '80's, yeah, exactly.

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:24.467
-But the Tom Petty sweatshirt
was because it was

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:27.334
a thick material and I was
always so insecure about

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:31.501
my shoulders being so skinny,
hence why I'm wearing a jacket.

00:01:31.501 --> 00:01:35.434
So I would pick wardrobe
for auditions to, you know,

00:01:35.434 --> 00:01:37.834
look a little full--
Listen, frankly, my shoulders

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:40.334
have been on back order
since the late '70s.

00:01:40.334 --> 00:01:41.467
-Okay. Alright. Yeah, okay.

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:43.567
-So, they're supposed to
come in this week.

00:01:43.567 --> 00:01:44.868
-But you're supposed to be
a kid that's going to get in

00:01:44.868 --> 00:01:46.801
shape enough to become
the Karate Kid.

00:01:46.801 --> 00:01:48.701
-Yeah, that's what I --
I don't know.

00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:51.767
I think maybe it was the only
thing that wasn't in the hamper.

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:52.801
-Yeah.
-Maybe that's why --

00:01:52.801 --> 00:01:54.367
-But you charmed
the director, though,

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:55.501
'cause you went --
The auditions were here

00:01:55.501 --> 00:01:56.534
in the Upper East Side, right?

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:58.000
-Yeah, Upper East Side.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.267
The late, great John Avildsen,
who directed

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:03.100
"Rocky" and "The Karate Kid"
and other great, great films.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.634
I went to his apartment,
and he said --

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:07.634
At the end of the audition,
he goes,

00:02:07.634 --> 00:02:09.601
"Listen, I can't guarantee
you anything,

00:02:09.601 --> 00:02:11.901
but if I were you, I'd start
taking karate lessons."

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:13.334
-Really?
-I was like, "Alright.

00:02:13.334 --> 00:02:14.934
That's pretty good
for the first date."

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.701
I was jumping-out-of-my-shoes
excited. I mean...

00:02:17.701 --> 00:02:19.601
-Pat Morita -- you have great
stories about that.

00:02:19.601 --> 00:02:22.400
That must have been emotional.
I know you miss him.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:25.267
-He was the soulful magic,
was the root of

00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:27.267
the secret sauce of
"The Karate Kid."

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:30.000
-People don't even know that
he did stand-up for a while.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.400
-No, he was a comic.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:34.501
He was the guy -- I was so
jealous of him back in the day

00:02:34.501 --> 00:02:37.100
because he would
do a scene about, you know,

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.601
internment camps
during World War II

00:02:39.601 --> 00:02:40.868
and Miyagi's backstory,

00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:43.067
and losing --
tragedy in his life.

00:02:43.067 --> 00:02:46.634
And then he would cut and he
would just lay into, like,

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:48.234
cross-eyed zingers
and fart jokes.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.267
And then he'd go --
When I would --

00:02:50.267 --> 00:02:53.334
I'd be like,
"I can't turn that on."

00:02:53.334 --> 00:02:55.534
I'd be like,
"I'm doing a dramatic scene.

00:02:55.534 --> 00:02:58.133
Everybody sit down,
clear the camera."

00:02:58.133 --> 00:02:59.534
You know? And so I was jealous.

00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:01.367
-But he almost
wasn't cast, right?

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:02.567
Because it was --
-Yeah.

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:05.267
No one in the studio wanted

00:03:05.267 --> 00:03:07.534
Arnold from "Happy Days"
as Mr. Miyagi.

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:10.167
It was just -- For all the --

00:03:10.167 --> 00:03:11.934
No one else
could have played that role.

00:03:11.934 --> 00:03:13.534
I mean, it was just --

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:14.634
-It was Jerry Weintraub?

00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:16.067
-Jerry Weintraub was like,

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:18.701
"There's no way I'm going to
have this guy in my picture."

00:03:18.701 --> 00:03:21.801
He wound up -- And then with
John Avildsen, the director,

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.834
and folks said --
And I was the same way.

00:03:23.834 --> 00:03:25.801
I was like, "You know, I don't
know about that," you know?

00:03:25.801 --> 00:03:27.767
We were all thinking of
the direction.

00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:33.501
But the moment I met Pat,
the moment we, you know,

00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:36.167
shared the yin and yang of it,
the give-and-take,

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:39.400
it was just
unconditional, genuine love.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:40.901
-And then Jerry was like --

00:03:40.901 --> 00:03:44.467
-Jerry was like, "Yeah, I made
the biggest mistake of my life.

00:03:44.467 --> 00:03:46.868
You got the part.
I was right all along."

00:03:46.868 --> 00:03:49.567
-Yeah. "I called it.
I knew you were the one."

00:03:49.567 --> 00:03:51.200
Yeah, he's the greatest.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.801
Everyone's talking about
"Cobra Kai."

00:03:52.801 --> 00:03:54.334
We're loving the new season.

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:56.534
We're wondering if there's
going to be another season.

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:57.601
We're hoping. There has to be.

00:03:57.601 --> 00:03:59.167
-Yeah, well,
we're counting on it.

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:02.801
It's not officially picked up,
so tell your friends,

00:04:02.801 --> 00:04:04.901
call your family, keep watching.

00:04:04.901 --> 00:04:06.567
-Write in to Netflix, an e-mail,
whatever you got to do.

00:04:06.567 --> 00:04:10.234
-Write and call your
congressman, senators, whatever.

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:12.834
I think -- We're feeling
really confident.

00:04:12.834 --> 00:04:14.567
-I think you're just
opening it up.

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:15.934
I mean, you're going
international now this season.

00:04:15.934 --> 00:04:18.501
-Yeah, that's the thing.
They've teed it up.

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:20.767
The writers of the show
are just so, so smart.

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:22.534
They've teed up the next level.

00:04:22.534 --> 00:04:25.334
Just when you think,
in this karate soap opera,

00:04:25.334 --> 00:04:28.567
all is well,
another door is going to open.

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:30.334
-Whatever it is,
do what you keep doing,

00:04:30.334 --> 00:04:31.801
keep it up,
because it is fantastic,

00:04:31.801 --> 00:04:33.100
what you're doing right now.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:35.067
We love you. Ralph Macchio!
I want to show a clip.

00:04:35.067 --> 00:04:38.734
Here's Ralph Macchio in Season 5
of "Cobra Kai."

00:04:38.734 --> 00:04:40.067
Take a look at this.

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:42.901
-Terry Silver --
this is how everyone sees him,

00:04:42.901 --> 00:04:44.434
as some kind of philanthropist

00:04:44.434 --> 00:04:45.868
out to save the kids
of the Valley.

00:04:45.868 --> 00:04:48.601
That's why you're here.

00:04:48.601 --> 00:04:50.601
I tried to stop Cobra Kai
on my own.

00:04:50.601 --> 00:04:51.601
Nothing's worked.

00:04:51.601 --> 00:04:54.200
There's only one way
to end this.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:56.267
We have to cut
the head off the snake.

00:04:56.267 --> 00:04:59.234
-Hai, Daniel-san.
I can do that.

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:03.400
-Whoa! No. No, no.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:06.067
I didn't mean
literally cut his head off.

00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:08.267
-They're not for cutting.

00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:10.767
They are for
blocking and stabbing

00:05:10.767 --> 00:05:12.601
and clawing and gouging --

00:05:12.601 --> 00:05:15.467
-Okay, please, put them away
before Amanda sees them.

00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:19.701
-Come on.
Ralph Macchio, everybody!

00:05:19.701 --> 00:05:22.734
Season 5 of "Cobra Kai"
is streaming now on Netflix.

00:05:22.734 --> 00:05:26.701
Check out his book, "Waxing On:
The Karate Kid and Me,"

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:28.000
out October 18th.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.701
We'll be right back with
Jennifer Beals.

00:05:29.701 --> 00:05:30.801
Stick around, everybody!

